{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"precranial-clerical-xiphias","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Problem\n\n`docs/experiments/calibrate_code_review_thresholds.py` cannot produce a trustworthy replay.\nCORRECTION (E) in `docs/experiments/code-review-threshold-calibration.md` records that it reads\nno routing index, so every re-run reproduces two known-wrong rows — `sec` reported as a\nDET/attestation gate (it is an LLM synonym of `security`) and `project.review-phase-boundaries`\nreported at the 0.95 unknown-criterion default rather than the 0.90 the project overlay sets.\nFixing it was deferred there.\n\nSeparately, `IMPACT_MODEL_VERSION` moved to **code-v5** on 2026-08-21\n(`src/rebar/llm/code_review/sidecar.py:35`), while the script's `--impact-model-version` still\ndefaults to a hardcoded `code-v3`. ADR 0036 forbids pooling across versions, so the default\nsilently analyses a retired cohort. No code-v5 calibration record exists in-tree.\n\n## Scope\n\n1. `docs/experiments/calibrate_code_review_thresholds.py` — read routing and label synonyms\n   through the production path (`registry.effective_routing`, `registry.normalize_criteria`)\n   with a pure-JSON fallback for checkouts where `rebar` is not importable; identify DET\n   criteria by their routing `exec` rather than a validity heuristic; default\n   `--impact-model-version` to the version the gate stamps today; print each proposal as a\n   DELTA against committed routing, showing UNROUTED distinctly from a deliberate advisory;\n   add `--dump-newly-blocking CRIT=THR`, which writes the findings a proposed flip would ADD\n   (priority in `[THR, current_threshold)`) to JSON for content adjudication.\n2. `docs/experiments/code-review-threshold-calibration.md` — mark CORRECTION (E) resolved,\n   describing what changed and the verification below.\n3. `docs/experiments/code-review-threshold-calibration-code-v5.md` — NEW. The calibration-4\n   record over the code-v5 segment: corpus and method, the per-flip adjudication, the severity\n   floor measured and rejected, the zero-impact analysis, the friction table, and corpus\n   hygiene. This is the artifact a later routing change cites.\n\nThis ticket changes NO gate behaviour: it touches only `docs/experiments/`.\n\n## Non-goals\n\nAny edit to `src/rebar/llm/code_review/criteria_routing.json` or to the tests that pin it.\nApplying the flips this record clears is sibling work that depends on this ticket.\n\n## Back-out\n\nRevert the three files; nothing else reads them at runtime.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] The generator is routing-aware: on the code-v3 segment it emits no `sec` row and no\n      `documentation` row (both normalize into `security` / `docs`).\n      Oracle: `python docs/experiments/calibrate_code_review_thresholds.py --tracker <checkout>/.tickets-tracker --impact-model-version code-v3`\n      produces no output line whose first field is `sec` or `documentation`.\n- [ ] The same run reports `project.review-phase-boundaries` at its overlay threshold.\n      Oracle: that run's `project.review-phase-boundaries` row shows `adv@0.90`, not 0.95.\n- [ ] The version default tracks the gate.\n      Oracle: `python -c \"import re;s=open('docs/experiments/calibrate_code_review_thresholds.py').read();assert 'default=\\\"code-v3\\\"' not in s\"`\n      exits 0, and a bare run (no `--impact-model-version`) prints\n      `[segmented to impact_model_version=code-v5]`.\n- [ ] `--dump-newly-blocking` writes the additive set.\n      Oracle: `python docs/experiments/calibrate_code_review_thresholds.py --tracker <checkout>/.tickets-tracker --dump-newly-blocking security=0.45 --dump-to /tmp/$$-nb.json`\n      exits 0 and the JSON key `security@0.45` holds only findings whose `priority` is\n      >= 0.45 and < 0.54.\n- [ ] CORRECTION (E) is marked resolved.\n      Oracle: `grep -c \"CORRECTION (E) — RESOLVED\" docs/experiments/code-review-threshold-calibration.md`\n      returns 1.\n- [ ] The code-v5 record exists and states its corpus size and method.\n      Oracle: `test -f docs/experiments/code-review-threshold-calibration-code-v5.md` exits 0 and\n      the file contains the corpus line and a per-flip adjudication table.\n- [ ] `make verify` is green.\n- [ ] The Gerrit change is MERGED (LLM-Review +1, Verified +1).","id":"2629-03a8-f93b-4457","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":["calibration","code-review"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Make the code-review calibration generator routing-aware and land the code-v5 record"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788906619370385001,"uuid":"b598a4fe-5da5-48ae-996c-ff91e3d7ed44"}